  "prompt": "Finance and Customer Success want both churn rates for each quarter of 2025, on one base. The base of a quarter is the accounts with MRR at the end of the quarter before: a row in mrr_monthly for the last month of the quarter before (December 2024 for the first quarter, then March, June and September 2025). The logo churn rate is the base accounts with a churn event (event_type churn in subscription_events) dated in the quarter, each counted once, divided by the base accounts. The MRR churn rate is the MRR lost to the base accounts' churn events dated in the quarter divided by the base's MRR (the sum of their mrr_eur in that mrr_monthly row). A churn event's lost MRR is its mrr_delta_local with the sign flipped, in euros: multiply by fx_rates.eur_per_unit for the subscription's currency on 2025-12-31, the rate mrr_eur uses. An account that started during the quarter is in neither rate. Return four columns, in this order: quarter_start (the first day of the quarter), accounts_at_start, logo_churn_rate and mrr_churn_rate, both as shares (0.02 for 2%), not rounded. Return one row for each quarter of 2025; a quarter with no churn shows 0. Any row order is fine.",
